# Advanced Multi-Platform Java CI with Ant
# Full documentation available at https://github.com

name: Java Enterprise CI

on:
  push:
    branches: [ "main" ]
  pull_request:
    branches: [ "main" ]

permissions:
  contents: read

jobs:
  validate-and-test:
    name: Test on ${{ matrix.os }} (JDK ${{ matrix.java-version }})
    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
    
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        os: [ubuntu-latest, windows-latest]
        java-version: ['17', '21']
        distribution: ['temurin']

    steps:
    - name: Check out repository code
      uses: actions/checkout@v6

    - name: Set up Java Environment
      uses: actions/setup-java@v4
      with:
        java-version: ${{ matrix.java-version }}
        distribution: ${{ matrix.distribution }}
        cache: 'ant'

    - name: Clean Workspace Targets
      run: ant clean -noinput -buildfile build.xml
      continue-on-error: true

    - name: Compile and Run Unit Tests
      run: ant test -noinput -buildfile build.xml

    - name: Package Distributable Binaries
      run: ant jar -noinput -buildfile build.xml

    - name: Archive Multi-Platform Build Artifacts
      uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
      if: success() && matrix.os == 'ubuntu-latest'
      with:
        name: enterprise-package-jdk${{ matrix.java-version }}
        path: build/jar/
        if-no-files-found: error
        retention-days: 7
Use code with caution.

Production Enhancements Included:

• Multi-Platform Matrix Execution: Runs your Ant targets simultaneously on both Linux (ubuntu-latest) and Windows (windows-latest) across both JDK 17 and JDK 21 to catch cross-platform compatibility bugs before they hit production.
• Deterministic Clean Steps: Integrates an ant clean execution boundary before compiling to prevent local caching corruption from leaking into runner image contexts.
• Optimized Storage Strategy: Restricts production artifact uploads to a singular, stable base target execution OS (ubuntu-latest) while systematically changing the upload artifact signature tag names by target version.
